Chapter 15
I rack my brain as much as I can to try and come up with a plan.
(t): I already tried shifting but it didn't work. Aimlessly flailing around didn't get me anywhere either.
I ponder what to do next and my thoughts wander to Scarlet again.
(t): I hope she's fine. What if the Spirits already let Amon loose in the present?
I shake my head to gain back my concentration.
(t): I have to get out of here. Now.
(t): The reason why I can't shift is probably because of the realm of the abyss. There must be some kind of spell or something that prevents me from using my shifting powers.
I think back to my training and try to find out if there are any clues that could help me escape.
(t): Right, I did master another power besides shifting. I can see Scarlet at any given moment if I close my eyes and think of her hard enough.
I decide to try it out immediately.
(t): If something abstract like shifting doesn't work, maybe having something I can visualise will help me find a way.
I close my eyes and purge my brain of anything except thoughts of Scarlet.
(t): There she is! I can see her with Ray, Seth and Lu.
They are sitting together right where I left them and appear to be safe. Though, Scarlet doesn't look very lively. It looks like she was crying and the others are trying to comfort her.
(t): But at least there are no Spirits in sight.
Just when I an about to sigh with relief I see how another portal opens, just like when the Spirits appeared earlier.
(t): No! They're already on it! I have to hurry!
I can only observe from where I am. The first person who steps out of the portal is Amon. He's followed by one cloaked Spirit, which I assume is the one I was with a little while ago.
(t): He's carrying his silver Sword! At this rate, the whole gang is in danger, And if they find the duke and the guards who have been locked up somewhere in there, then the problem will grow even bigger.
I open my eyes to focus on finding a solution again. I only see darkness.
(t): My power of visualisation still works in this space. But when I want to do something like shifting, which I did so much that I don't really think about it anymore, then this realm somehow blocks the power.
(t): Wait a minute.
A sudden thought pops into my head.
(t): Portals! They're something I can visualise, and as the Sustainer of dimensional Principles, the one who should have the ability to conjure up something like that should definitely be me. Why haven't I thought of that before?
I take a deep breath.
(t): Okay. If those Spirits can do it, I can do it too.
I concentrate and try to feel the powers within me.
(t): I just have to imagine it first.
I see it in my inner eye. I see the outline of my arm.
I stretch out my arm and imagine the powers within me plowing out, creating a similar mist like those spirits, just prettier and not as menacing. It sparkles and looks magical.
The mist swirls around in front of me. I move my arm with it, as if stirring it.
Soon it creates an oval. The portal is almost complete.
(t): Wow, it feels so real. I don't know if I'm imagining it anymore or if this is reality.
I think of the place where I want the portal to take me.
(t): Maybe the power of a Sustainer is shaping their imagination into reality.
And with that thought, I step into the portal.
I'm immediately blinded by a bright light.
(t): Agh! My eyes!
