Once my eyes have adjusted I see that I'm back in the base of the gang.
I did it! I found another way to cross dimensions!
With a newfound confidence I step further ahead and realise what's happening right in front of me.
Amon is trying to get to Scarlet who is still not in a condition to fight, while the trio is defending her.
The Spirit just looms around in the corner, but yells out after noticing me.
???: How is this possible?!
Me: I'm back, guys!
Amon and the others turn to me with surprised faces.
Scarlet: {playerName}! I'm so glad you made it back safely! How could you just leave like that after confessing your feelings! Didn't you suspect that those weird Spirits would go behind your back and do whatever they want?
Me: You're right, I'm sorry. But at that time, you literally had a dagger pointed at you so I had to do what I had to do. And I'm here now.
Amon looks irritated.
Amon: Hey you, demon or whatever you are. Didn't you say there was no escaping that place?
He looks at the Spirit with annoyance glimmering in his eyes.
???: The Sustainer must have evolved somehow. I don't know how this could happen.
Then they both look at me.
What? What are they looking at?
???: Then I'll just have to end this right here, right now.
Amon: In the end, I always have to do everything by myself.
I pause and look at them, trying to see which one will attack first.
But all of a sudden, they both sprint in my direction at the same time, ready to attack me.
I have learned that visualisation is important, so I quickly conjure up a shield the same way I did with the portal.
That was close!
I manage to ward the both of them off, but they keep launching attacks toward me.
Their hits are heavy and I feel like the shield won't hold against them much longer.
Especially the magical attacks of the Spirit are unlike anything I've seen before.
I struggle to keep my balance under the shield.
Now that I think about it, maybe the Spirits have merged together into one being, because this one seems a bit bigger than the ones I've seen until now.
Damn, two versus one is a little unfair, isn't it? What should I do?
I decide to call the others for help.
I am not alone. I have allies too!
I manage to keep the shield up while I imagine a weapon that could defeat these two.
Well, Amon won't be too hard, since he's a normal human. But the Spirit probably needs to be killed with a power equal to their own.
A sword, the blade infused with my powers. Or would a sturdy club be better? Or a bow with infused arrows. Maybe a gun with infused bullets is best.
I imagine all these weapons but I am interrupted by a cracking sound coming from the shield.
Crap!
I focus and conjure them up next to the others who stayed back observing the chaos.
They notice them and seem to grasp immediately what they should do next.
Ray grabs the club, Seth the sword and Lu takes the bow and arrows. Finally Scarlet firmly grips the gun and they position themselves behind Amon and the Spirit.
I have full confidence that this will work. I trust them and I trust my vision.
The enemies don't notice anything. They are fully focused on breaking the shield.
Just as the cracking sound from my shield becomes more frequent and it is on the verge of breaking, the others ambush them from behind.
The trio attacks the spirit and Scarlet shoots Amon.
Wait! Scarlet will end up killing Amon again!
The Spirit explodes and there is no trace left of it. I can't even feel its presence anywhere near. Amon just sinks to the ground.
The shield crumbles and disintegrates into thin air.
Me: Phew! That was a close one, thank you guys.
Scarlet: I'd kill him a hundred times over if it means saving you.
Lu sadly looks to the ground while Seth solemnly wipes the dust away from his clothes.
Ray: But boss! Wasn't the goal of that whole fiasco that you don't have to kill him anymore?!
I laugh.
Me: Don't worry guys. He's alive.
We look over and see Amon flat on the ground, occasionally twitching in pain.
It's good that I have gained an even more precise control of my powers.
Everyone looks at me with puzzled faces.
Seth: How is that possible?
Scarlet: I— I shot him though! with this gun! And I don't think I missed.
Me: It's true. It may look like you shot him directly in the heart, but remember, this weapon was created by me. It's only natural that I would be able to erase its existence.
Lu: Woah…
Me: And I did just that with the bullet. Just as it was about to hit his heart and deal a fatal blow on that bastard. Though, it did manage to knock him out.
I look at Scarlet.
Me: So, you're officially not a murderer. If you want, I can take on that role for you.
Ray: Nah! Let me finish him off!
Seth: Calm down, Ray. That silver sword of his wounded us. We should treat our injuries and leave this to them.
Lu: I agree… I have a cut here that burns. I need a band aid. And a blood pack.
Scarlet lets out an exhausted sigh.
Scarlet: Seth is right. You three, go get yourselves treated first. And you, {playerName}, you should get treated as well. Forget about Amon. The most important thing is that we are together again and this time in safety.
She comes closer and hugs me.
Although this takes me by surprise, I hug her back tightly and savour the moment.
This is what I fought for. This must be true happiness.
When I pull back, Scarlet suddenly draws my face close and plants a kiss right on my mouth, catching me by surprise yet again.
She gently caresses my cheek while we kiss.
When we part our lips I notice the others staring at us in disbelief. Ray's jaw is practically on the floor.
Me: What's this sudden burst of affection?
I look at Scarlet and can't help but grin from ear to ear.
But internally I'm screaming of joy.
Scarlet: It's my answer to your confession. My way of saying “I love you too”.
While we look at each other all lovey-dovey, I completely forget about the unconscious Amon on the ground.
Seth: Ahem. I really don't want to interrupt this special moment, but he's still there. And your father and his guards are here as well.
Scarlet: Oh, right. Somehow, they escaped from the confinement rooms.
I glance to the back of the room and see the duke with his guards peeking over.
Did I just get kissed in front of my father in-law? How embarrassing!
Scarlet: Father. Do you see what his intentions were now? Still willing to give your daughter to him?
Mr. Moon: I see now that I should never have gotten involved with this man.
Scarlet: Then that's all that counts.
It seems like she could finally get through to him.
CHOICE OPTION 1: I can't wait for our future together.
